-- title:
--   Products by generators preserve the lower-weight span
-- statement:
--   If each coefficient polynomial lies in the complex span of the lower-weight monomials, then the sum of its products with the corresponding generators lies in their span over the algebra generated by those generators. Use that each generator belongs to the adjoined algebra, and close the module span under scalar multiplication and finite sums.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

import Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic
